			<div class="content" id="post-content-1613861">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Explanations&nbsp;for&nbsp;those&nbsp;who&nbsp;desire&nbsp;them</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;ABLE&nbsp;FREEMAN</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>So Kondraki and Light had been plotting to take down Clef for some time now, because he's a super dangerous person. Epon and Able got added to the list, as the three of them could cause some major damage.</p>
<p>They used Kondraki's butterflies to fake the kumiho escaping, to lure Clef into a killzone they had set up with agents they had brought to their cause. Fats, Nemo, and their guys never got there, as Able broke up their strike teams whilst wandering about and the loyalist agents had realized what went on (yes, all of that happened off screen, I know, I know). Kondraki was using the Katana of Apparent Invincibility, though it's uselessness wasn't actually known at the time. Most of his dialogue there is taken from a /tg/ copypasta called &quot;Katanas are underpowered in d20&quot;.</p>
<p>This whole failed incident will then become known as the Chaos Insurgency, as evidenced by the tale title.</p>
<p>Also, it should be noted that Ukulele seems to be slipping back, without outside command. That ain't good.</p>
</div>
